 "title": "What a Home EV Charger Install Really Involves #shorts",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "Thinking about a Level 2 EV charger at home? Here's what a proper install actually involves."
  },
  {
   "text": "Step one is a load calculation. We check your electrical panel to see if it can handle the charger on top of everything else in your house."
  },
  {
   "text": "That answer decides the cost. Panel capacity, how far the cable has to run, and whether you need a panel upgrade."
  },
  {
   "text": "Step two is the permit. In Loudoun and Fairfax County, an EV charger needs an electrical permit and an inspection."
  },
  {
   "text": "Skip it, and you could have problems with insurance or when you sell the house."
  },
  {
   "text": "Step three, set up off-peak scheduling, so the car charges overnight when power often costs less."
  },
  {
   "text": "Load calc, permit, off-peak. NovaProHome handles all three. Free quote at novaprohome.com."
  }
